From 3c8c42f497d7a04b4b5e521542f66aa3b77567bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Cl=C3=A9ment=20Gayot?= <contact@clement-gayot.fr>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 14:26:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(shader): never redirect actors that contain the window
 groups

GNOME Shell keeps global.window_group and global.top_window_group
inside Main.uiGroup, not on the stage.  OverlayManager put the shader on
every stage child except window_group, which in practice meant on
uiGroup itself, i.e. around the window groups.  MetaWindowGroup paints
through mutter's culling, which goes wrong inside an offscreen
framebuffer, and windows also carried their own effect:

- the desktop background dropped out of the dimmed image whenever the
  screen changed, so the screen flickered between dimmed and black
  (reported on a 144 Hz + 60 Hz dual-monitor setup);
- windows were dimmed twice (brightness squared).

Put the shader on uiGroup's children instead, skipping the
MetaWindowGroups and the cursor-clone group, plus every window actor
and the background groups; follow uiGroup child additions/removals.

Since the effect now sits on actors of many sizes, monitor targeting no
longer uses stage-relative UV rects, which were also wrong for window
actors before.  GammaCurveEffect picks the brightness at paint time
from the stage area being painted (one monitor's view, or a screencast
of it), recovered from the framebuffer viewport, so the shader is a
plain multiply.

Also:
- the cursor clone is no longer inside a dimmed actor, so it dims its
  own sprite by texture color modulation (brightnessAt() honours the
  monitor selection);
- paint targets that paint nothing (empty containers such as
  modalDialogGroup) without the effect, instead of letting
  ClutterOffscreenEffect allocate a zero-sized framebuffer;
- skip remove_effect() on effects Clutter already detached during
  destruction ("not attached" warnings).
